Package: prismrepl
Title: Snappy and Rich Terminal Console
Version: 0.6.4
Authors@R: person("Alek", "Rutkowski", email = "alek.rutkowski@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Provides an opt-in interactive console with multiline editing,
    syntax highlighting, completion, searchable history, object inspection,
    documentation browsing, and readable condition traces. A small native
    terminal layer supports Linux and macOS terminals and the Windows console.
    A responsive full-screen interface combines a transcript, editor, and workspace sidebar,
    with buffered rendering, mouse navigation, persistent preferences,
    structural object exploration, a searchable command palette, file browsing,
    function editing, clipboard support, styled documentation, labeled conditions,
    matching delimiter colors, automatic pairing and configurable browser links
    for error explanations. Initial themes follow detected desktop appearance. Plain
    console operation is available when terminal capabilities are limited.
    No external interpreter, service, or network connection is required.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/alekrutkowski/prismrepl
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.5.0)
Imports: cli (>= 3.6.0), processx (>= 3.8.0), rlang (>= 1.1.5),
    stringi (>= 1.7.0),
    utf8 (>= 1.2.0), methods, stats, utils, tools
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.2.0), withr, roxygen2, rcmdcheck, remotes
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
NeedsCompilation: yes
SystemRequirements: C99
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
